truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.19+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Restrict the relaxed :identifier suffix to host NQNs only (#44
    follow-up). _nvme_untaint_cli_nqn is shared by both host and
    subsystem NQN validation; making the suffix optional also silently
    accepted suffix-less subsystem NQNs, which the NVMe-oF spec still
    mandates. New require_identifier flag defaults to required; only
    the host-NQN call site opts out.

 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Sat, 04 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.18+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Relax NVMe host NQN validation to accept NQNs without :identifier
    suffix (#44). Per NVMe-oF spec the :identifier segment is mandatory
    for subsystem NQNs but optional for host NQNs. The Linux kernel
    generates host NQNs as nqn.YYYY-MM.tld.domain with no further suffix;
    the previous regex rejected them with "Invalid NVMe host NQN", making
    NVMe-TCP completely non-functional for affected hosts. Fix makes the
    :identifier block optional in _nvme_untaint_cli_nqn; malformed NQNs
    and shell metacharacters are still rejected.

 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Thu, 03 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.17+deb1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Template / linked-clone support (plan C). Implements the PVE
    template lifecycle end-to-end for both iSCSI and NVMe-TCP:
      - parse_volname recognizes base-<vmid>-disk-N and the
        slash-encoded "<base_volid>/<clone_volid>" form used by
        linked clones.
      - create_base renames vm-<vmid>-disk-N to base-<vmid>-disk-N
        (pool.dataset.rename force=true), rewires the transport
        share to the new zvol path, and snapshots the base as
        @__base__. The iSCSI extent's naa and the NVMe namespace's
        device_uuid/nguid stay stable across the rewire, so PVE's
        /dev/disk/by-id and /dev/disk/by-path entries do not change.
      - clone_image defaults snapname to __base__ when the source
        is a base image, and both _clone_image_iscsi and
        _clone_image_nvme now return the slash-encoded volname so
        PVE records the parent relationship in the clone VM config.
      - volume_has_feature advertises clone => {snap,base} and
        template => {current}; the misleading clone => {current}
        (which caused "clone not supported without snapshot") is
        removed.
      - free_image refuses to destroy a base while any linked clone
        still derives from its @__base__ snapshot. The check queries
        pool.dataset.query filtered by origin.parsed (TN's
        pool.snapshot.query does not surface the ZFS `clones`
        property in this release).

  * NVMe create_base ordering fix. TN validates the current
    device_path on every namespace.update, including {enabled:false}.
    Renaming first invalidated the path and blocked the disable;
    disabling first while the old path is still valid succeeds.
    New order: disable → rename → rewire → re-enable, with
    symmetric rollback paths that re-enable the namespace on failure.

  * volume_rollback_is_possible: implement to refuse rollback to a
    non-latest snapshot, matching ZFSPoolPlugin semantics. Previously
    volume_snapshot_rollback silently destroyed newer snapshots via
    recursive=1 (required by TN 25.10 rollback semantics), which
    tripped disk_snapshot.pl test 9 ("snap1 and snap2 still present
    after rollback"). PVE now blocks the request at the ORM layer.

  * disk_purge.pl test 9 fix. After a purge, a different pvedaemon
    worker's stale mapping cache still lists the vanished volume.
    Two-part fix: clear the mapping cache on the purging worker
    after delete, and in _list_images_iscsi treat the fresh
    pool.dataset.query result as ground truth — skip any
    targetextent mapping whose backing zvol no longer exists.

 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Mon, 29 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.16+deb1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Critical fix in _iscsi_rescan_sd_capacity: was reading
    $scfg->{target_iqn} instead of $scfg->{tn_target_iqn}. On this
    branch the storage.cfg key is tn_target_iqn (the tn_ rename
    landed in v2.1.0); the bare name returns undef, so the helper
    fell through "return unless length $iqn" and did nothing. Every
    call site wired into alloc_image / _clone_image_iscsi /
    activate_volume since v2.1.14 has been hitting a no-op.
    Multi-disk full clone failures with "qemu-img: output file is
    smaller than input file" continued in v2.1.15 because the
    intended SCSI READ CAPACITY rescan never ran on the recycled
    sdX. Single-character fix.
    Introduced by my cherry-pick of e9e8441 onto this branch: the
    call-site conflicts were resolved to use tn_use_multipath but
    the same rename inside the helper body was missed.

 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Fri, 26 Jun 2026 14:00:00 +0000

truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.15+deb1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Critical fix to _is_connection_error: remove the /x regex flag that
    silently turned every multi-word alternative in the connection-error
    pattern into a no-match. With /x, "broken pipe" compiles to
    "brokenpipe", "WS read" to "WSread", "connection reset" to
    "connectionreset", etc. None of the real-world errors matched, so:
    - _api_call did NOT invalidate stale persistent WS connections on
      framing/EPIPE failures
    - _is_retryable_error returned 0 for connection errors, so the
      retry-with-backoff path never fired
    - storage status mis-marked transient connectivity as
      non-recoverable
    Cascade: when the persistent WS goes stale, the next preflight
    sequence (core.ping + service.query + dataset.get + ...) all
    inherited the broken cached connection. Each sub-check failed with
    "WS write failed: Broken pipe" or "WS read hdr failed" and the
    plugin gave up without ever reconnecting.
    The /x flag was introduced by fe06ea1 ("fix: classify WS framing
    errors as connection errors for reconnect"); fix is to drop /x and
    keep the pattern on one logical line. Also adds "WS write" to the
    alternation so write-side failures classify the same way.

 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Fri, 26 Jun 2026 11:00:00 +0000

truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.14+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Force SCSI READ CAPACITY on iSCSI sdX devices when LUN numbers are
    recycled. When an iSCSI extent is deleted and a new extent reuses
    the same lunid, the kernel retains the same sdX block device with
    the OLD (smaller) capacity. iscsiadm -m session -R discovers new
    LUNs but does not refresh capacity on existing sdX entries. qemu-img
    convert during a multi-disk full clone then sees a destination
    smaller than the source and aborts with "output file is smaller
    than input file". New _iscsi_rescan_sd_capacity helper writes 1 to
    /sys/block/sdX/device/rescan for every iSCSI-backed sdX in the
    plugin's target_iqn session. Wired into alloc_image's deferred
    block, _clone_image_iscsi's deferred block, and activate_volume.
    Cheap, idempotent. Cherry-picked from broker-service e9e8441.
  * Add --start N / --stop M flags to the dev-truenas-plugin-full-
    function-test.sh runner and a diagnostic dump on multi-disk clone
    failure (by-path symlinks, base+clone VM config, blockdev sizes per
    proxmox-lun-*, TN iscsi.extent.query). Optional KEEP_ON_CLONE_FAIL=1
    leaves state for inspection. Cherry-picked from broker-service
    50414b8.

