  * Implement LXC vzdump snapshot mode support (issue #42): activate_volume,
    path, and deactivate_volume previously ignored the snapshot name and
    returned the live block device, failing snapshot-mode backups. The plugin
    now clones <zvol>@<snapname> into an ephemeral zvol and exposes it as its
    own iSCSI LUN / NVMe-TCP namespace, tearing it down in
    volume_snapshot_delete (and deactivate_volume as a fallback).
  * Fix NVMe namespace lookup using the wrong query field: nvmet.namespace.query
    nests the subsystem under subsys.id (subsys_id is create-only input).
    Namespace lookups now query by the unique device_path; the namespace
    counter in _free_image_nvme filters by subsys.id.
